ligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054373 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054373 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $9^1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054373 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93e87899-2b3f-5a97-9a86-538b1acc34b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054373 #edb/ref 1074 "Any number raised to the first power is itself. So $9^1 = 9$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Product Using an Exponent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054842 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "40e41bd9-1eee-552d-8507-e8cdf50ddfa4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating an Exponential Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054843 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "85e60062-7218-5aab-a67a-2cc84f7ad973" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054844 #edb/ref 1039 "Raising a Number to the Power of One" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054844 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054844 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1f2cde7b-5f1d-57d0-b24c-c215d83a1936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1045 "Exponents With Rational Bases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054878 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "1741802a-ec50-5bf7-99b5-64889f83ba7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055097 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186052018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055097 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055097 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 3$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055097 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "32ed6c57-e38f-563f-ad32-4eac3ae02fef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186052887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-43207" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055275 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $(-\\frac{2}{3}) \\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}) \\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}) \\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3})$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d895c26-f8e3-5adb-bbd3-a7c7c3d0ff8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055897 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055897 #edb/ref 1061 74297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055897 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb689754-aa8e-5f1a-bf8d-0c16cbd2123a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055897 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055898 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055898 #edb/ref 1061 74298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055898 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9014a35-b28c-5285-9282-5aba8ec6ac64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055898 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055899 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055899 #edb/ref 1061 74302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055899 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "54b5575d-a602-5aa6-b10e-76a946359f7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055899 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055900 #edb/ref 1061 74306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055900 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "156590f0-8245-5a72-b5e9-95d4b42d678f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055900 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056006 #edb/ref 1064 "We've already seen that $5^2$ means $5\\cdot 5$, and that $5^3$ means $5\\cdot 5 \\cdot 5$. We can extend this to have any number in the exponent, for example\n\n$$\n5^{\\color{blue}7} = \\underbrace{5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5 \\cdot 5}_{\\large{\\color{blue}7} \\textrm{copies of} 5}\n$$\n\nThe **exponent** $({\\color{blue}7})$ says how many times the **base** $(5)$ is multiplied by itself.\n\nRecall that $5^2$ is said as \"five squared\" and that $5^3$ is \"five cubed.\" We don't have special names for larger exponents. However, we can say $5^7$ in several different ways:\n\n- \"five raised to the seventh power,\"\n- \"five raised to the power seven,\"\n- \"five to the seventh power,\"\n- \"five to the power seven.\"\n\nRaising to the power of one is special. Any number raised to the first power is itself. For example, $5^{\\color{blue}1}$ means one copy of $5$, so\n\n$$\n5^{\\color{blue}1} = 5\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056006 #edb/ref 1065 8020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056006 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "964b1381-44c4-5a32-832a-ec441cc4a890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056006 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
